## Exam Relevance & Objectives

In the Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) exam, candidates are frequently tasked with configuring new human users:

1. Generating private keys and CSRs with specific Common Names (`CN`) and Groups (`O`).
1. Submitting a Kubernetes `CertificateSigningRequest` (`certificates.k8s.io/v1`).
1. Approving the request with `kubectl certificate approve`.
1. Extracting and decoding the issued certificate from `.status.certificate`.
1. Registering credentials (`kubectl config set-credentials`) and contexts (`kubectl config set-context`) in `~/.kube/config`.
1. Verifying authorization failures and binding targeted `Role` or `ClusterRole` objects.

